WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.189
A rental page can look convincing while its address or water supply is wrong.

00:00:06.189 --> 00:00:14.589
ScoutVault lets a buyer ask someone nearby to check it, review a signed report, and release a small bounty.

00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:19.453
Here is a labelled sample studio listing in Akoka, Lagos.

00:00:19.453 --> 00:00:24.316
It advertises an address, a price, and a water tank.

00:00:24.316 --> 00:00:26.413
Paste the link.

00:00:26.413 --> 00:00:32.004
Firecrawl captures the page and proposes three checks.

00:00:32.004 --> 00:00:38.994
The buyer can edit the questions and choose the entrance.

00:00:38.994 --> 00:00:43.886
The public map shows an approximate pin.

00:00:43.886 --> 00:00:47.851
Review the reward and network costs before funding.

00:00:47.851 --> 00:00:52.312
These are project-issued test tokens with no cash value.

00:00:52.312 --> 00:00:55.782
Solana makes a small token bounty practical.

00:00:55.782 --> 00:01:03.217
The Anchor program holds two tokens for this check and limits who can move them.

00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:06.920
Switch to the scout and claim the check.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.698
Only one scout can claim it.

00:01:09.698 --> 00:01:13.864
Supabase stores nearby checks and the private audit trail.

00:01:13.864 --> 00:01:16.642
The written checklist is the default.

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:22.660
Play brief reads it aloud when a browser or device voice is available.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.923
Answer each question and attach a report.

00:01:25.923 --> 00:01:30.585
The app supports a fresh camera capture and location permission.

00:01:30.585 --> 00:01:34.314
I am using the labelled sample illustration here.

00:01:34.314 --> 00:01:38.043
This recording does not claim a site visit.

00:01:38.043 --> 00:01:41.306
Seed Vault protects a phone wallet's keys.

00:01:41.306 --> 00:01:45.035
It does not certify the camera or GPS.

00:01:45.035 --> 00:01:51.112
The scout signs the report and submits its hash.

00:01:51.112 --> 00:01:58.538
ScoutVault checks the original photo bytes, report hash, and wallet signature.

00:01:58.538 --> 00:02:09.340
The buyer reads the answers, sees what could not be confirmed, and approves this exact report.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.507
The scout receives two test tokens.

00:02:13.507 --> 00:02:23.229
Here is the actual payout in Solana Explorer, connected to the local demonstration validator.

00:02:23.229 --> 00:02:30.000
Public devnet activation and a physical Seeker test remain pending.
